      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Palace of Culture and Science, a Soviet‑era skyscraper, dominates Śródmieście’s skyline and houses theaters, offices, and a museum.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/%C5%9Ar%C3%B3dmie%C5%9Bcie%2C_Warsaw",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Łazienki Park, a royal park in Śródmieście, hosts the Palace on the Isle and a famous Chopin concert hall for open‑air performances.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/%C5%9Ar%C3%B3dmie%C5%9Bcie%2C_Warsaw",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The University of Warsaw, founded in 1816, sits in Śródmieście and is one of Poland’s oldest higher‑education institutions.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
